+\'93It\'92s in my DNA?\'94\
+Janine nodded. Her cheeks flushed. She smiled and shed a tear and stretched her legs and scratched an itch at the back of neck. She let out a hoarse moan that released tension from parts of her body she hadn\'92t had any reports from in months. \'93Oh, yes!\'94\
+Pin Cushion hugged her Mum until her Mum could probably lay assault charges.\
+\'93So I\'92ll live to I\'92m old? Like fifty or something?\'94\
+Janine chuckled. She leaned in and, a little above a whisper, said, \'93Probably a century more than that.\'94\
+\'93What?\'94 Pin Cushion processed. \'93So now I\'92m a different kind of freak?\'94\
+Janine kissed her forehead. \'93I expect it will commonplace in the not-too-distant future.\'94\
+\'93Okay, right. I\'92ll be a commonplace freak then.\'94\
+They sat in silence for a while.\
+\'93We can talk more about this tomorrow. How about we just celebrate tonight. I\'92ll order delivery.\'94\
+\'93I want barbecued chicken.\'94\
+\'93Really?\'94\
+\'93Yeah, I feel like I can take on one of those cluckers, now that I don\'92t waddle like them any more.\'94\
+Janine fished her tablet out of her bag and got to ordering. \'93Coleslaw?\'94\
+\'93You know I do. Also, can I have a bike? Or, if we can\'92t afford one, I\'92d settle for a monocycle.\'94 Pin Cushion knew they could afford one.\
+\'93Will you just stop already?\'94 Janine asked, with out rancour.\
+\'93I\'92m happy, Mum.\'94\
+\'93Me too.\'94\
+\'93I love you too, Pin\'97\'94 Janine caught herself. \'93I love, Sarah.\'94
+\f0\fs24 <!$Scr_Ps::1>}
