-\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_H::2>
-\f0 Riding an exercise bike requires extensive engagement of the pelvic girdle and the proximal lower limb muscles (specifically the gluteus maximus, quadriceps, and hamstrings). Because 
-\f2\b Limb-Girdle Muscular Dystrophy (LGMD)
-\f0\b0 specifically targets and destroys these muscle beds first, Sarah\'92s ability to ride a bike is the ultimate clinical confirmation for Janine.\
-Janine will be watching for three specific mechanical signs that the TPlus virus has permanently integrated into Sarah's satellite cells:\
-\
-\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
-\ls1\ilvl0
-\f2\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
-\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Eradication of the Gowers' Sign Profile:
-\f0\b0  A child with LGMD lacks the pelvic floor strength to transition from sitting to standing without physically using their hands to "walk" up their own legs. Janine watches Sarah push herself up off the bike seat effortlessly using only her thighs.\
-\ls1\ilvl0
-\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
-\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Fluid Kinetic Symmetry:
-\f0\b0  There is no asymmetric hitching of the hips or dropping of the pelvis to compensate for weak muscle groups. The cadence of her pedaling is smooth, circular, and consistent.\
-\ls1\ilvl0
-\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
-\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Anaerobic Threshold Shift:
-\f0\b0  Thanks to the spliced 
-\f2\b vent fungi and anaerobic pathways
-\f0\b0  in the TPlus platform, Sarah isn't lactic-acid burning or gasping for air. Her muscles are utilizing oxygen with extreme, engineered efficiency. She is exerting real force but breathing like she is at rest.\
