+\'93You already told me.\'94\
+\'93It\'92s the largest we\'92ve ever put in a person before.\'94\
+Pin Cushion had practice at playing the adult in the room. It came with all the clinical ceremonies she mostly had to just wait out in silence. \'93So I\'92m a lab rabbit.\'94\
+\'93More like a lab princess.\'94 Janine managed a weak laugh.\
+\'93Mum, everyone\'92s life is a test run.\'94\
+A tear ran down Janine\'92s cheek. \'93You had to grow up so fast.\'94\
+\'93One of us had to.\'94\
+Janine started to laugh, but choked it back.\
+\'93Mum. Give me the juice.\'94\
+That made it harder. Pin Cushion was a child, not matter much she\'92d had to grow up before her time. Janine knew the decision was hers. She drew a breath. Clinically, she was confident she was right. \'93Okay.\'94\
+The needle went in; Pin Cushion hissed through her teeth. \'93Fuck.\'94\
+Janine looked at her daughter through her eyebrows as she slowly delivered the dose.\
+The second injection hurt more.\
+Afterwards Pin Cushion sat up and inspected both dressings. \'93I\'92m disappointed. I expected glowing.\'94\
+Janine checked her pulse.\
+Janine checked her blood pressure.\
+Then oxygen saturation. Then temperature. Then pulse again.\
+She sat beside her daughter and waited. Ten minutes\'85 twenty.\
+Pin Cushion complained that her thigh hurt. Pain at the injection sites was ordinary. Ordinary had become magnificent.\
+At forty minutes Pin Cushion said, \'93I\'92m hungry.\'94\
+Janine made toast and slathered it with an industrial-sized quantity of Vegemite, the way  Pin Cushion liked it. She was like that with chilli too, as if extreme flavours demonstrated she\'92d survive, despite it all.\
+At an hour, Janine checked everything again.\
+That evening Pin Cushion developed a headache and complained that both legs felt heavy. Janine took blood twice and made her drink water until she gargled and feigned choking on it.\
+Pin Cushion went to bed annoyed and alive.\
+Janine sat outside her room for another hour.\
+
